\name{LatticeSmoothLayerProcessor}
\alias{LatticeSmoothLayerProcessor}
\title{lattice Smooth Layer Processor}
\description{
Reads the curves lattice computes while it draws as a \code{smooth} layer,
one series per group: the density estimate of a \code{densityplot()}, and the
loess, spline and least-squares fits of \code{xyplot(type = "smooth")},
\code{"spline"} and \code{"r"}.

The curve is read off the drawn grob rather than computed again: it is
the curve the panel function drew, whatever bandwidth, span or limits it
was given. A least-squares fit is drawn as one segment, clipped to the
panel, and is read as its two ends.

The observations \code{densityplot()} draws under its curve -- jittered
points or a rug -- are the data again rather than the reading, and are
left out, as the curve is what the chart is drawn to show.
}
\keyword{internal}
